# Deploying Shell and Remotes Independently in Angular NX Module Federation

## Introduction

One of the biggest advantages of Module Federation is:

```text
Independent Deployment
```

Without Module Federation:

```text
One Application
One Build
One Deployment
```

With Module Federation:

```text
Shell
Customer Remote
Admin Remote
Reports Remote
```

Each application can be built and deployed independently.

This is one of the primary reasons large enterprises adopt Micro Frontend Architecture.

---

# Traditional Monolithic Frontend

Suppose we have:

```text
Customer Module
Admin Module
Reports Module
Settings Module
```

inside a single Angular application.

Structure:

```text
apps/
|
└── portal
    |
    ├── customer
    ├── admin
    ├── reports
    └── settings
```

---

## Deployment Process

A small change is made in:

```text
Customer Module
```

Even then:

```text
Build Entire Application
Deploy Entire Application
```

is required.

---

## Problems

```text
Long Build Times
Long Deployment Times
Higher Risk
Large Teams Block Each Other
```

